# Utah Teapot: the 32 bicubic Bezier patches of the 1987 version with the
# rounded bottom (Frank Crow, 1987; the classic lidded shape after Martin
# Newell and Jim Blinn), 4 x 4 control points per patch.
#
# Source: https://graphics.cs.utah.edu/teapot/ (University of Utah). Its terms:
# the Utah Teapot model files are freely available for any use, including
# commercial use; the model and versions derived from it are to be credited
# as a "Utah Teapot" (or "Modified Utah Teapot").
#
# Operandi's own format (read by crates/operandi-core/src/teapot.rs):
# "points N", then N lines "x y z" (z up, spout toward +x); "patches 32",
# then one line per patch of 16 point numbers, row by row. The control
# points were recovered exactly from the site's own patch tessellation
# (cubic Bezier samples at 0, 1/3, 2/3, 1 solve back to their control
# points); the values are the classic data's, to four decimals.
